# DroidDeck venus-bridge guest driver: the environment this driver needs.
#
# The app reads this when the driver is selected and adds it to the session after its own
# defaults and before the user's droiddeck-env, so a line here is the driver's own setting and
# nothing on the phone has to be edited to change it. One NAME=value per line; "#" starts a
# comment.
#
# This file is the ONLY place a driver knob is stated. The APK sets no driver knob of its own --
# it used to add DROIDDECK_VN_SYNC_PRESENT itself, and that line is gone -- so changing one of the
# settings below means shipping a driver, never an APK build.
#
# A line in the user's droiddeck-env file is applied after this one and wins, which is deliberate:
# every on-device A/B here is an edit to that file (DROIDDECK_VN_SYNC_PRESENT=0 restores the fast
# path, DROIDDECK_VN_EMULATE_BC=0 disables the decode), so a knob the user's file could not
# override would leave shipping another driver as the only way to test it.
#
# Present ordering (guest-patches/0021). The queue drain before every present is skipped and the
# present is ordered by this submit's ring seqno instead: a wait for the host to execute through
# the submit, not for the GPU to go idle. =1 is the ordered present; =0 is the fast path with no
# ordering at all.
DROIDDECK_VN_SYNC_PRESENT=1
#
# BC textures are decoded on the GPU (guest-patches/0024). On by default; stated so the zip
# records which decode it carries.
DROIDDECK_VN_BC_GPU=1
#
# ---- Diagnostics. Uncomment one line, push, and CI builds a driver that carries it, so the test
# ---- is a driver install and not an edit on the device.
#
# The test that decides the frame collapse: BC emulation off. The textures that needed decoding
# stay empty, so the picture is wrong on purpose; the "frames:" line is the measurement (back to
# ~50 fps means the BC path is the collapse).
#DROIDDECK_VN_EMULATE_BC=0
#
# The pacing lever: uncap the nested refresh from the session's 60 Hz to the panel's 120 Hz.
# Steam's UI can overrun at 120 Hz ("Fatal IO error 11").
#BL_MALI_REFRESH=120
#
# The other end of the present A/B: no ordering before the present.
#DROIDDECK_VN_SYNC_PRESENT=0
#
# BC7 on the GPU. Off by default: BC7 is 1.4% of the compressed bytes, so it cannot move the
# frame rate, and the black-texture reports came after it shipped on.
#DROIDDECK_VN_BC7_GPU=1
#
# The A/B for the frame collapse (guest-patches/0026). The BC decode's two dispatches are ordered
# with scopes that name only the stages that touch the buffers (host/transfer -> compute, compute
# -> transfer). =1 puts back the ALL_COMMANDS -> ALL_COMMANDS barrier it used to record, which on a
# tile-based GPU flushes the tiler per upload. Back to ~50 fps with this unset and 2-10 fps with it
# set means the tiler flush was the collapse.
#DROIDDECK_VN_BC_COARSE_BARRIER=1
